Feature: TC_13_STAFF - Active Farmer System Notes E2E Regression Pack

  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Legacy  : "Regression Pack for Active Farmer History Notes" (BISSAGL-7777, AT-TC-01 to 03,
  #           tmslinks BISSAGL-14850 / 14842 / 14840)
  # Rewritten 16-10-2026 in the StaffSteps vocabulary (the wording the MAPS features run with). One end-to-end
  # scenario; # SECTION markers show where each legacy scenario starts.
  #
  # Purpose:
  #   Every Active Farmer admin check action writes a system note to the History tab, word for word:
  #     - starting the check applies the "Admin Check in Progress" stop
  #     - approving the check lifts the stop, with the admin note as the comment
  #     - rejecting, appealing with evidence and then approving lifts the stop with the appeal note
  #   Each note must be dated today, so a note left by an earlier run on the same herd does not count.
  #
  # Legacy coverage notes carried forward:
  #   - AT-TC-02 approved the check that AT-TC-01 had started on the same herd (row 2); Section 2 returns to that herd
  #     explicitly instead of relying on scenario order.
  #   - The appeal evidence is Test_Data/Cover_Letter.pdf (legacy uploaded a file from a local Windows folder).
  #
  # Test data:
  #   Herds from the database, as in legacy ("Herds with Admin Check Not Started", scheme year 2024) - each run
  #   needs herds whose admin check has not started, which a fixed herd cannot give twice.
  #   Login agr4442 (BISS Co-ordination 1). Password: TD:Password from the TestData row of this test case.
  #
  # Step definitions: stepdefinitions.BISS.STAFF.StaffSteps (Active Farmer, History)
  # Author: Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Background:
    Given the staff user is logged in to the BISS internal portal as "agr4442"

  @regression @staff @active-farmer @admin-check @appeals @e2e
  Scenario: AT-STAFF-ADMIN-NOTES-E2E-01 - Staff runs the Active Farmer admin check and appeal and checks each system note

    # SECTION 1 : Start the admin check - the stop is applied - AT-TC-01 (BISSAGL-14850)
    When the staff user opens the Active Farmer screen for the next admin-check herd for scheme year "2024"
    And the staff user starts the active farmer admin check
    Then the application history should record "Active Farmer Admin Check in Progress Stop has been Applied with comment: Admin check started manually" today

    # SECTION 2 : Approve the same check - the stop is lifted - AT-TC-02 (BISSAGL-14842)
    When the staff user returns to the Active Farmer screen for the same admin-check herd for scheme year "2024"
    And the staff user completes the admin check with the following result
      | result | APPROVED  |
      | notes  | Test Note |
    Then the application history should record "Active Farmer Admin Check in Progress Stop has been Lifted with comment: Test Note" today

    # SECTION 3 : Reject, appeal with evidence, approve - the stop is lifted - AT-TC-03 (BISSAGL-14840)
    When the staff user opens the Active Farmer screen for the next admin-check herd for scheme year "2024"
    And the staff user starts the active farmer admin check
    And the staff user completes the admin check with the following result
      | result | REJECTED  |
      | notes  | Test Note |
    And the staff user raises an appeal with supporting evidence
    And the staff user completes the admin check with the following result
      | result | APPROVED        |
      | notes  | Appeal Approved |
    Then the application history should record "Active Farmer Admin Check in Progress Stop has been Lifted with comment: Appeal Approved" today
